{"name":"Programs: get as a thin node","description":"Test demo: a thin node connects, downloads a signed program by address, verifies it and runs it","kind":"thin","entry":"thin.txt","args":["10.0.2.2:7020","03e489240a78d8a85713f5b6d22749632d8268e238c40b9aca99f54c44de11828d","2be5b3ae0178b0aabca390bafce9b8c521a0ec4f2dc21c8afb5b257e5f2dc12d"]}This app holds no program. It is a thin programnetwork node: it connects
to the node its args give, downloads the program at the manifest address
its args give, checks the signer key of its args and every block hash, and
is done, with no subscription and nothing kept. Then it runs the program.
See "Node types (#34, #44)" in docs/ProgramDistribution.md.
